{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788187280,"nonce":"yNcCq8TsRPMh+4DkcpgzMWdcIbg=","title":"assign needs an auto_arm lever — nothing can turn FSWA auto-arming on","message":"The third combat-readiness control, and the only one with no route at all.\n\nThe set, after 2026-08-31:\n\n  1. seek-at-will {on, stance}          — BUILT this session (SeekAndKill)\n  2. assign {hostility:\"Attack\"}        — shipped in 3.4\n  3. auto-arm on                        — NO VERB EXISTS\n\nFindSuitableWeaponAndAmmo (dorian.findsuitableweaponandammo) is per-pawn opt-in\nauto-arming: an opted-in pawn equips the best available weapon and re-arms when\ndisarmed. The toggle is a checkbox in the ASSIGN TAB — which is exactly the\ncolumn strip 3.4's `assign` verb already reproduces — plus a gizmo.\n\nSo the natural shape is a new lever on the existing verb:\n\n    assign {pawns:[…], auto_arm:true}\n\nAPI, read from the mod's source rather than guessed:\n  AutoArmTracker.IsAutoArm(Pawn) / SetAutoArm(Pawn, bool)  — on a GameComponent\n  (AutoArmTracker.cs:31,41); `AutoArmTracker.Get =\u003e Current.Game?.GetComponent`\n  MpSync has a sync path for player actions; check whether SetAutoArm is one of\n  the sites it wraps before calling it directly (MpSync.cs, and see FSWA issue\n  e82e399 \"MP: sync player actions\", which is still open).\n  The gizmo is Command_ToggleAutoArm (SidearmGizmos.cs:174), and\n  HarmonyPatches.cs:203 shows the click path:\n  `SetAutoArm(pawn, !IsAutoArm(pawn))`.\n\nMOD-AWARE, like seek-at-will. FSWA is not a dependency. Take no compile-time\nreference; reflect, cache, and report cleanly when the mod is absent. SeekVerbs.cs\nis now the in-repo template for this — including the mistakes its review caught:\nbind by SIGNATURE not name alone, never swallow a reflection throw into a legal\nstate value, and read the write back rather than assuming it took.\n\nTHE STANDING ORDER THAT COMES WITH IT: unforbid dropped weapons. FSWA skips\nforbidden ones explicitly (FSWA_MapComponent.cs:80,\n`thing.def.IsWeapon \u0026\u0026 !thing.IsForbidden(Faction.OfPlayer)`) and raider drops\nland forbidden. Evan caught this live on a map holding an unused forbidden\nrifle, revolver, knife and full flak set. A direct `equip` order BYPASSES\nforbidden, which is what masks the problem — the manual path works while the\nautonomous one silently does nothing. 3.2's `unforbid` is the fix; the play\nloop (4.2) should do it after every raid.\n\nAcceptance\n\n- `assign {pawns:[…], auto_arm:true|false}` toggles it, gated like every other\n  assign lever, with the before/after read BACK from the tracker.\n- Absent mod: the lever is refused with a named reason, not an exception, and\n  the rest of the assign call still applies.\n- `pawn`'s state or assign's `after` publishes current auto-arm state so it can\n  be checked without setting it.\n- Demonstrated: an unarmed colonist with auto_arm on, an UNFORBIDDEN weapon on\n  the map, and an advance — pawn ends up holding it, with no `equip` order in\n  the journal.\n- The weapon-choice quality itself is FSWA's problem, not ours: see its issues\n  f512ec0 (role from traits/skills/passions) and 8070f34 (non-CE defaults).","files":null}]}